[5.85778, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5.859637, "o", "# Billing — plan changes, invoices and GST\r\n\r\nAll money is integer paise. Plans and prices live in `billing/plans.py`.\r\n\r\n## §1 Billing periods\r\n\r\nA subscription is billed per period `[start, end)`. Monthly periods are anchored on the\r\nsubscription's day of month (clamped to short months); annual periods run 12 months from\r\ntheir start date. Day counts are actual calendar days, so February has 28 or 29.\r\n\r\n## §2 Changing between monthly plans\r\n\r\nA customer can switch monthly plans on any day `on` inside the current period. Let\r\n`unused = days from on (inclusive) to period end` and `D = days in the period`:\r\n\r\n* credit = old monthly price × unused / D\r\n* charge = new monthly price × unused / D\r\n* the billing period is unchanged.\r\n\r\nEvery prorated amount is rounded **half-up** to the nearest paisa.\r\n\r\n## §3 Upgrading from a monthly to an annual plan (PAY-412)\r\n\r\nA customer on a monthly plan can upgrade to an annual plan on any day `on` inside the current\r\nmonthly period:\r\n\r\n* **Credit.** `credit = old monthly price × unused / D`, using the same `unused` and `D` as §2,\r\n  rounded half-up to the paisa.\r\n* **Charge.** The full annual price of the new plan.\r\n* **Net.** `net = charge − credit`.\r\n* **New period.** The annual period starts on `on` (`annual_period(on)`).\r\n* Only monthly → annual is an upgrade. Any other combination (annual → anything, monthly →\r\n  monthly) raises `ProrationError`, as does an `on` outside the current period.\r\n\r\nThe result is a `ProrationResult` (`billing/proration.py`).\r\n\r\n**Invoice.** An upgrade invoice shows the annual plan's charge line followed by a credit line\r\nfor the unused part of the monthly plan:\r\n\r\n    Proration credit: <old plan name>, <unused>/<D> days\r\n\r\nwith amount `−credit`. The credit line appears only on invoices that carry a proration.\r\nProrated lines are taxed per §5 like any other line.\r\n\r\n**SAC column (all invoices).** GST rules for credit lines require the services accounting code\r\non every invoice line, so PAY-412 also adds a SAC column to **all** invoices. Every line row\r\nshows its SAC code — `998314` for all of our services — between the description and the\r\namount. Row layout: description cut to 43 characters and left-aligned in a 44-character column\r\n(the last column stays blank, as today's 45-in-46), SAC right-aligned in 8, then\r\nAmount (12), GST (11) and Total (11) right-aligned as today, so invoices become 86 characters\r\nwide; the header row gains a `SAC` heading and the rules and totals widen to match.\r\n\r\n## §4 Invoices\r\n\r\nAn invoice lists its billable lines; each line is taxed separately (§5) and the invoice\r\nshows subtotal, GST and total due. `billing/invoice.py` renders invoices as text.\r\n\r\n## §5 GST\r\n\r\nGST at 18% is computed **per line** and rounded **half-up to the nearest paisa**: an exact\r\nhalf paisa always rounds away from zero (`₹0.225 → ₹0.23`, `₹0.235 → ₹0.24`,\r\n`−₹0.225 → −₹0.23`). Invoice GST is the sum of the line amounts.\r\n"]
[5.860008, "o", "\r\n--- proration ---\r\n"]
[5.862051, "o", "\"\"\"Mid-cycle plan changes (SPEC §2 monthly changes, §3 upgrades to annual).\"\"\"\r\n\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\r\nfrom datetime import date\r\nfrom decimal import ROUND_HALF_UP, Decimal\r\n\r\nfrom billing.periods import Period, annual_period, remaining_days\r\nfrom billing.plans import Plan, get_plan\r\n\r\n\r\nclass ProrationError(ValueError):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass ProrationResult:\r\n    old_plan: Plan\r\n    new_plan: Plan\r\n    on: date\r\n    period: Period  # the old plan's current billing period\r\n    unused_days: int\r\n    credit: int  # paise credited for the unused part of the old plan (>= 0)\r\n    charge: int  # paise charged for the new plan\r\n    new_period: Period\r\n\r\n    @property\r\n    def net(self) -> int:\r\n        return self.charge - self.credit\r\n\r\n\r\ndef prorate_amount(price: int, days: int, period_days: int) -> int:\r\n    \"\"\"``price * days / period_days`` rounded half-up to the paisa.\"\"\"\r\n    exact = Decimal(price) * days / period_days\r\n    return int(exact.quantize(Decimal(\"1\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef prorate_monthly_change(old_code: str, new_code: str, period: Period, on: date) -> ProrationResult:\r\n    \"\"\"Switch between two monthly plans inside the current period (SPEC §2).\r\n\r\n    The customer is credited for the unused days of the old plan and charged for\r\n    the same days of the new plan; the billing period does not move.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    old, new = get_plan(old_code), get_plan(new_code)\r\n    if old.is_annual or new.is_annual:\r\n        raise ProrationError(\"monthly changes only; use prorate_to_annual for annual upgrades\")\r\n    unused = remaining_days(period, on)\r\n    return ProrationResult(\r\n        old_plan=old,\r\n        new_plan=new,\r\n        on=on,\r\n        period=period,\r\n        unused_days=unused,\r\n        credit=prorate_amount(old.price, unused, period.days),\r\n        charge=prorate_amount(new.price, unused, period.days),\r\n        new_period=period,\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\ndef prorate_to_annual(old_code: str, new_code: str, period: Period, on: date) -> ProrationResult:\r\n    \"\"\"Upgrade from a monthly plan to an annual plan on ``on`` (SPEC §3).\"\"\"\r\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"annual-plan proration is not implemented yet (PAY-412, SPEC §3)\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef describe(result: ProrationResult) -> str:\r\n    return (\r\n        f\"{result.old_plan.name} -> {result.new_plan.name} on {result.on.isoformat()}: \"\r\n        f\"credit {result.credit}, charge {result.charge}, net {result.net}\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\n__all__ = [\r\n    \"ProrationError\",\r\n    \"ProrationResult\",\r\n    \"describe\",\r\n    \"prorate_amount\",\r\n    \"prorate_monthly_change\",\r\n    \"prorate_to_annual\",\r\n]\r\n\r\n--- Makefile ---\r\n"]
